---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL } from '../lib/site.js';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="RigFloorHQ sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser. This page explains exactly what that means and how to verify it yourself."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookie Policy', href: '/cookies' }]}
  lang="en"
  alternateHref="/es/cookies"
>
  <Nav slot="nav" lang="en" alternateHref="/es/cookies" />
  <Footer slot="footer" lang="en" />

  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="page-hero-eyebrow">Legal</div>
    <h1>Cookie <span>Policy</span></h1>
    <p class="page-hero-sub">This site does not use cookies. Here is what that means, and how to check it yourself.</p>
    <div class="page-meta">
      <span class="page-meta-item">Last updated <strong>{LEGAL.lastUpdated}</strong></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="prose">
      <div class="note-box">
        <strong>{SITE.name} sets no cookies.</strong> Not necessary ones, not analytics
        ones, not advertising ones. Nothing is written to your browser's cookie store,
        local storage or session storage. That is also why you have never seen a cookie
        banner here.
      </div>

      <h2>What a cookie is</h2>
      <p>
        A cookie is a small file a website asks your browser to store, so it can recognise
        your browser on a later page or a later visit. Related technologies — local
        storage, session storage, pixels and fingerprinting — do much the same job by
        different means. Together they are how most of the web remembers who you are.
      </p>

      <h2>What we use</h2>
      <p>
        None of it. There is no cookie table on this page because there are no cookies to
        list. Specifically, this site does not use:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Strictly necessary cookies</strong> — we have no logins, baskets or preferences to remember, so none are needed;</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics cookies</strong> — we run no analytics product at all, so we do not know how many people visit or which pages they read;</li>
        <li><strong>Functionality cookies</strong> — the language switch works by linking to a different URL, not by storing a preference;</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising or targeting cookies</strong> — we carry no advertising and are not part of any ad network;</li>
        <li><strong>Local or session storage</strong> — the calculators run entirely in the page and keep nothing once you navigate away.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why there is no cookie banner</h2>
      <p>
        Under UK and EU rules a site must obtain consent before storing anything on your
        device that is not strictly necessary. We store nothing, so there is nothing to ask
        you about. A banner here would be theatre.
      </p>
      <p>
        It also means there is no consent choice for you to manage, change or withdraw —
        a "cookie settings" link would have nothing to control.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party requests</h2>
      <p>
        One thing does leave your browser: our pages load typefaces from Google Fonts.
        Google receives your IP address and browser details in order to serve the font
        files. Google states it does not set cookies on the Google Fonts service, but the
        request itself is a transfer of data to a third party and we would rather name it
        than leave it out. This is covered in more detail in our
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Beyond fonts, our pages make no third-party requests — no analytics beacons, no ad
        calls, no embedded video, no social widgets, no maps.
      </p>

      <h2>Check it yourself</h2>
      <p>
        You do not have to take our word for any of this. In your browser, press
        <span class="highlight">F12</span> to open developer tools, then look at the
        <strong>Application</strong> tab (Chrome and Edge) or <strong>Storage</strong> tab
        (Firefox). Under Cookies, Local Storage and Session Storage for this domain you
        will find nothing. The <strong>Network</strong> tab will show you every request the
        page makes.
      </p>
      <div class="note-box">
        <strong>Worth knowing.</strong> If you ever find a cookie set by this domain, that
        is a bug or a change we failed to document — either way we want to hear about it at
        <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.contactEmail}`}>{LEGAL.contactEmail}</a>.
      </div>

      <h2>If this changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we ever add analytics or advertising, we will update this page with a full table
        of what is set and why, update the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, and put a
        proper consent banner in place before anything non-essential is stored. Nothing
        will be switched on quietly.
      </p>

      <p style="font-size:13px;">
        See also our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>,
        <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> and <a href="/about">About</a> page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
